# Components & folders

## Layers

| Layer     | Path                    | Use for                                 |
| --------- | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| `ui/`     | `src/components/ui`     | Primitives, no business logic           |
| `shared/` | `src/components/shared` | Composed widgets used on multiple pages |
| `views/`  | `src/components/views`  | Page/feature-specific UI                |
| `layout/` | `src/components/layout` | Shell (header/footer)                   |

## Prefer UI primitives

Always check `src/components/ui` before using raw HTML interactive elements. Prefer existing primitives (`Button`, `Input`, `Checkbox`, `Link`, `Dropdown`, `Multiselect`, `DualRangeSlider`, …) over native tags.

- Style via the component API (`variant`, `size`, `customClass`, icons props) — do not reimplement with raw `<button>`, `<input>`, `<a>`, etc.
- Native elements are OK only when no UI primitive fits, or when implementing inside a `ui/` primitive itself.
- Import via barrels (`@/components/ui/button`).

```tsx
// ❌
<button type="button" onClick={onRemove} className="px-3 py-1 rounded-lg ...">
  {label}
</button>

// ✅
<Button size="small" customClass="w-fit ..." handleClick={onRemove}>
  {label}
</Button>
```

## New component package

Always:

```
feature-or-component/
├── index.ts          # public barrel
└── components/       # implementation
```

Add `types/`, `hooks/`, `utils/`, `constants/` **only when needed** (no empty folders).

## Exports & imports

- Components: **default** export + barrel re-export.
- Hooks / types / utils / enums / constants: **named** exports.
- Import only via barrel: `@/components/ui/button` — never `@/components/ui/button/components`.
- For enums, types, interfaces, and constants: declare first, then export at the **end** of the file (no inline `export enum` / `export type` / `export interface` / `export const`).
- Re-export types with the `type` keyword in the export list.

### Naming: `type` vs `interface`

- **Component props / context contracts:** `interface` with **`I` prefix** (`IButton`, `IFiltersPanelContext`).
- **Aliases, unions, picks, domain shapes:** `type` with **`T` prefix** (`TFiltersForm`, `TFilterOption`).

```ts
// ✅
interface IPriceFilter {
  priceMin: string;
  onChange: (min: string, max: string) => void;
}

type TFiltersForm = {
  priceMin: string;
  material: string[];
};

// ❌
type TPriceFilter = { ... };
interface TFiltersPanelContext { ... };
```

```ts
// ✅
import Button from '@/components/ui/button';
import Filters from '@/components/shared/filters';

enum MaterialEnum {
  canvas = 'canvas',
}
type TFilterOption = {
  value: string;
};
export { MaterialEnum, type TFilterOption };

// ❌
import Button from '@/components/ui/button/components';
export enum MaterialEnum {
  canvas = 'canvas',
}
```

- Exception: Next.js `export const metadata` / `export const config` stay as framework requires.

## File naming

- Component files: **PascalCase** (`FiltersTrigger.tsx`, `Headline.tsx`, `Mobile.tsx`).
- Hooks: `useX.ts`. Folders: kebab-case.

## One component per file

- **Never** define more than one React component in a single file.
- Each component gets its own PascalCase file (default export).
- Helpers that are not components (hooks, utils, constants, types) stay in their own folders — do not co-locate extra components as “private” siblings in the same file.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — FilterGroup + RangeField + Content in Content.tsx
// ✅ GOOD — FilterGroup.tsx, RangeField.tsx, Content.tsx
```

## New page checklist

1. Thin `src/app/.../page.tsx` (metadata + data + Suspense).
2. Feature under `src/components/views/<feature>/`.
3. Include Suspense + Loading fallback + page metadata.

